If you're planning a new website or marketing materials and need a logo, timeline matters. Here's an honest picture of how long the process typically takes — and what affects the pace.

## The typical timeline

For most logo projects with NC Digital, the process takes **one to two weeks** from briefing to final delivery. Here's how that breaks down:

**Brief and discovery** — We start with a brief: your business, your audience, the look and feel you're aiming for. This is usually a short conversation or a questionnaire. Time: 1–2 days.

**Initial concepts** — We produce 5 initial logo concepts for you to review. Time: 3–5 working days.

**Revisions** — You choose a direction and we refine it based on your feedback. One to two rounds of revisions is typical. Time: 2–4 working days.

**Final delivery** — Once approved, we prepare all file formats and deliver everything. Time: 1 day.

## What can slow things down

The biggest variable in any logo project is decision-making time on the client side. If you review concepts quickly and give clear feedback, the process moves fast. If there are multiple decision-makers who need to align, or if the brief changes direction mid-project, timelines extend.

Coming to the project with a clear sense of what you like — even if that's just a collection of other logos you admire — helps keep things moving.

## If you need it faster

For genuinely urgent projects, get in touch and explain your timeline. We'll be upfront about whether we can accommodate it.

## Combining with a website project

If you're also having a website built, we can often run the logo and website design in parallel — the logo is completed and handed over in time for it to be incorporated into the website design. See our [web design service](/services/web-design/) for more on how those projects work together.

Learn more about the process in [what to expect when you commission a logo design](/blog/what-to-expect-when-you-commission-a-logo-design/), or [get in touch](/contact/) to discuss your project.
